  "description": "teenage engineering OP-Z: every control of its guide's incoming MIDI table, the per-track parameters on the track's channel.",
  "sources": [
    {
      "type": "manual",
      "title": "OP-Z guide: midi",
      "notes": "The guide's MIDI table, read by tools/profiles/teenage/read-te-guide.mjs from the page https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-z/midi as saved on 2026-11-10 (sha256 f4bfdb398f94b44377cf732049b9ac89cbc8c879b108767270805e5a0e47077e). A guide is a live page: a later one may differ. Not yet checked against the instrument itself."
    }
  ],
  "testedWith": [],
  "authoringNotes": [
    "Generated by tools/profiles/teenage/make-profiles.mjs; edit the layout in tools/profiles/teenage/synths/, not this file.",
    "Every parameter is a row of the guide's table of incoming MIDI control changes, with its printed name, sent as that controller. Nothing here has been sent to a real instrument yet.",
    "The channel variable is the track's: each of the OP-Z's 16 tracks has its own channel (1 - 16 by default), and its parameters answer on it. Set it to the track to edit; the rows marked `any` answer on every channel.",
    "The guide prints a second set of controllers, 32 - 49, that step the same parameters up or down (1, 127); they are not laid out.",
    "Rows on a controller already laid out, named here, not laid out: next pattern (CC 103, 16), previous pattern (CC 103, 17).",
    "Left out by the layout (see its comment): CC 51 TRACK GAIN (RELATIVE), CC 102 active track, CC 102 parameter page."
  ],
